Happ compatibility key data
===========================

The legacy RSA keys and the first 34 crypt5 compatibility keys were imported
from happwn:
https://github.com/useruserdev/happwn
Revision: 8ae0171535a1622f100a1535a216afbe7675d58d
Files: rust/data/pkcs1_keys.json, rust/data/expanded_rsa_keys.json
License: Apache-2.0 (included in happ-keys.LICENSE).

The additional crypt5 protocol key values for markers asajzqxt and vdfzfoff
were obtained from the published compatibility table in Happ Link Decryptor:
https://github.com/LeeeeT/happ-decryptor
Revision: 5a05cfe59f45db8684be26077ce28979a3ee3208
File: public/data/crypt5-keys.json
That project does not specify a source-code license. Only the two RSA key
values (protocol compatibility data) are included; no code was copied.

These are publicly distributed application compatibility keys, not user
credentials. User subscription URLs and tokens must never be added here.
The table covers crypt through crypt4 and 36 crypt5 markers. New markers
require a table update; unknown markers fail closed.

Wire-format references:
https://github.com/useruserdev/happwn/blob/8ae0171535a1622f100a1535a216afbe7675d58d/docs/crypto.md
https://leeeet.dev/happ-decryptor/

Tachyon's framing and OpenSSL adapter in happ.uc are a separate implementation.
